WEBVTT

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.810
TRIGGER will perform on the first 
day of the inaugural concert,

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:06.370
and we're thinking of having 
IDOLiSH7 perform on the second day.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.860
Iori will be the center instead of me?

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.940
Just think of me as our pinch-hitter 
until you've fully recovered.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.860
My lover is my fans.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.460
I never do anything to sadden my fans.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.080
I never break promises I make to my fans.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.320
You can't keep promises.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.790
I'll never recognize you as an idol.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.440
I hate you... Tenn-nii.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.840
My head hurts...

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.670
Don't make that face just because 
your little brother hates you.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:41.560
He doesn't hate me.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.810
No, he definitely does after all 
that horrible stuff you said to him.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.460
He <i>doesn't</i> hate me.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.900
Just suck it up and accept it.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.740
All this from the man who got shot
 down twice within five minutes?

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.450
I wasn't hitting on her!

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.450
Please don't yell.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.790
I'm sorry, okay? I'll try not to drink too much.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.960
I hope those boys are okay.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.220
Come in.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.930
Hey, TRIGGER.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.970
We brought you some very fun news.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.520
Discover...

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.740
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:34.810
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.150
Wow...

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:50.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:55.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.530
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:06.250
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.930
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.470
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.880
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:18.430
Discover...

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:27.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.240
Night sky

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.110
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.580
There's a glimmer I want to realize with you

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:41.160
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.450
Wow...

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.870
My head hurts.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.280
I drank too much.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.780
Here, have some water. Are you all right?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.000
Thank you.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.390
Thanks.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.370
Oh, right. Re:vale came over last night.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.590
Banri-san, you said you were a fan of theirs... 
Maybe I should've invited you over.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.290
I appreciate it.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.840
More importantly, where's Nanase-san?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.210
Good morning, guys!

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.720
Let's do our best again today!

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.220
That's some obviously fake energy.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.060
It's not fake! I <i>am </i>energetic!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.110
Today I'm going to do a perfect job, 
sing until the end, and make Tenn-ni—

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.800
Make Kujo Tenn acknowledge me!

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.460
Ever since we were kids, Tenn-ni—

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:40.240
Kujo Tenn would always tell me, "Don't do this, 
don't do that, don't ever do that."

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.660
And I haven't had any attacks recently,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.930
so I'll show him I can do it!

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.740
Well, don't push yourself too hard.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.610
We're us.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.120
Instead of seven perfect guys, 
let's be perfect together as seven.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.460
Mitsuki.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.160
The great MC sure has a knack for words.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.620
Don't be stupid. It's not like that.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.690
Anyway, our new song goes on sale tomorrow.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.590
I hope we make it onto the 
singles ranking chart.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.050
Good morning.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.250
Good morning.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.600
Morning...

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.560
D-Did something happen?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.110
Shinbashi

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.110
You said you were in Shinbashi...

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.740
Sorry, I forgot.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.360
But nothing happened, right?

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:22.920
I hate So-chan.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.990
He's always saying, "Don't do this,
don't do that, don't ever do that."

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:29.230
<b>As someone more
 mature than you</b>

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.230
Tamaki, don't be so childish!

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.520
Come again, Nanase-san?

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.770
Other people always come first, 
and I get pushed aside!

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:35.360
I didn't have a choice.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.000
They've helped us as our seniors 
and said they wanted to eat them!

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.470
You <i>totally</i> had a choice!

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:45.220
You know I love King Pudding, but you
 still prioritized Yukirin and Momorin!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:48.210
I <i>told</i> you, I'll buy you more today 
and I apologized last night.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:50.410
That's not the problem!

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.540
It's about how I feel!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.980
Besides, using money to solve the problem 
makes you seem like a bad rich guy!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.000
A bad—

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.350
Shut up!

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:04.780
Last night, they refused to listen to my pleas
 for them to stop and dropped my figure!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:08.080
Oh, poor Cocona.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.120
I should have kicked these 
devils out of my room sooner.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.290
S-Sorry, Nagi-kun.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.820
You should be apologizing to Cocona, not me!

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.170
Sorry, Cocona-chan.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.050
Come on, Tamaki-kun.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.690
Only after you apologize to me!

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.300
I've apologized a bunch 
of times since last night!

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.730
Silence, you devils!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:32.180
Now, now. That's enough arguing.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.170
Good morning.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.230
You two...

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.270
Huh? What's going on?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:41.070
Ah, don't worry about it. 
So, what are we discussing today?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:46.570
Re:vale's agency contacted us regarding 
the Zero Arena inaugural concert.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.490
To discuss what?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.430
On the final day of the inaugural concert,

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:53.640
they plan to celebrate the fifth 
anniversary of Re:vale's formation.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:58.250
They'd like us to perform 
as a surprise guest.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.130
What? At Re:vale's concert?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.390
Oh!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.750
Better not bring any pudding. They'd eat it.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:08.130
Not only that, but they've made special 
plans for us to form special units with TRIGGER.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.230
What? With TRIGGER?

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.390
Special units, huh?

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.650
I'm surprised my dad allowed that.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.640
We planned it in secret.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.610
We've got a bunch of other ideas, too.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.400
Don't want to?

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.900
No. If it's work, we'll do it.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:28.270
You're as cold as ever. I love it.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.530
By the way, Tenn, we heard 
your dad's in Japan.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:34.250
Hey, introduce us to him already.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.630
What are you, my fiancé
of five years, or something?

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:41.230
It's your fault for concealing 
your private life!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.960
Momo-san, what are your other plans?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.630
That's still a secret.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.630
Regarding Re:vale, we've 
received a formal offer.

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:55.310
I see. I had no intention of accepting it, 
but you made some valid points.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:58.390
Re:vale is a top idol group in 
both name and substance.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:02.480
The media will be paying attention, and 
there are merits to having TRIGGER perform.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.870
You're right.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:09.050
Besides, I can't have them running wild with
scissors and screaming gibberish at me again.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:10.560
What are you talking about?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.990
It's a private matter!

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:16.350
Kujo-san has expressed interest 
in the inaugural concert, as well.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.120
What? He has?

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:24.130
Genius stage director and specialist 
in star development, Kujo Takamasa.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:27.630
Apparently, he's training one in secret now.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.000
I'd like to have them debut with us.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.240
And for that reason,

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.570
it's not a bad idea to increase TRIGGER's 
exposure at the inaugural concert.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:39.770
New talent? I wonder what 
they'll be like this time.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:44.820
There's a particular reason Kujo-san 
is so interested in the Zero Arena's

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.770
inaugural concert.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.530
A reason?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.410
Hey, Kaoru-chan.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.620
Hello.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.640
You boys...

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.520
I told you not to come here.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.580
Loosen up a little!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:07.880
Anyway, how did your presentation 
with Papa Yaotome go?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.770
It's going well.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:14.130
You've helped our boys, and I'm 
glad we could be useful to you.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.510
Good girl.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.600
Spare me the flattery.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.700
More importantly, do you have the goods?

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:24.060
We've got it! A limited-edition Nagi photo!

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.060
To: Kaoru-chan

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.070
No way! It even has his 
autograph and a kiss mark!

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.400
And this one's not for sale!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.670
Oh, my gosh! It's so cute! My prince!

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.910
I think I'm gonna cry!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.560
It feels so exquisite...

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.860
You should just be honest 
and admit you're a fan.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:38.860
He's so precious...

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.770
I could never say that!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:44.590
I'm a woman who keeps her professional 
and private lives separate!

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:48.140
Come, Nagi-kun. Let's go home together.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.490
I'm glad you seem happy.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:51.340
Yeah.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:55.340
Anyway, I heard the news. Is it true?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.800
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.010
We'll tell you the details tomorrow.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:03.310
Good morning.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.230
We look forward to working with you today.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.850
<b>Okazaki Productions</b>

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:06.270
Yeah.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.850
So do we.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:11.480
We're truly delighted to 
be working with TRIGGER.

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.180
Though we may cause some trouble for you, 
we truly appreciate this opportunity.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:23.370
O-Of course, we'll do our best 
not to cause any trouble.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.400
Um...

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.630
Tsumugi, you're so earnest.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:30.540
Huh?

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:33.100
I like that about you.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.300
Hold up.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.470
Could you not hit on our manager?

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.800
Y-Yamato-san?

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.970
And you need to be careful 
not to fall for any bad men.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.550
Hey, what does that mean?

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:47.920
I bet you're a real playboy, yeah?

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.200
I am not!

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:51.390
What? You're not?!

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:53.860
If <i>you're</i> not, then who is?!

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:57.030
You should apologize to all the guys 
who dream of having their own harems!

00:09:58.040 --> 00:09:59.600
S-Sorry.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:00.690
Good.

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:02.680
Wait, why am I apologizing?!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.000
Hiya, thanks for waiting.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:06.710
Re:vale.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.980
Sorry. Our recording ran long.

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:11.580
To make up for it, I'll escort you.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.210
Wh... What?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.730
Back off!

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:17.470
They're right. Leave her be, okay?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.450
Allow me to introduce you.
This is our manager.

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:23.470
Normally he can't make it to our jobs.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:24.630
Nice to meet you.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:29.100
I'm Re:vale's manager, Okazaki 
Rinto of Okazaki Productions.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.520
Manager

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.880
Thank for coming all the way here today.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:33.320
It was no problem at all.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.190
Manager

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.190
Nice to meet you.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:40.340
I'm IDOLiSH7's manager, Takanashi 
Tsumugi of Takanashi Productions.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.450
The two of them have been very kind to us.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.950
Is that right? I hope they're 
not causing any trouble.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.620
Absolutely not. Right?

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:51.330
Yes. Thank you for everything.

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.660
I hope you'll continue working with them.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:56.510
That's enough introductions.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.060
I'll show you inside.

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.300
Okay.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.390
Kaoru-chan, I'll escort you.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.770
Well, I don't mind this much at all.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:07.640
I'd be happier with a blond-haired 
blue-eyed beauty, though.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.290
Oh, sorry!

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.230
But I'm plenty charming, too, right?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:17.150
Yaotome-san and Nikaido-san, 
allow me to escort you!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.260
No thanks.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.240
<b>Meeting Room C</b>

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.860
This is the tentative plan 
for the special units.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.870
<b>2. The project concepts

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:25.870
Not bad.

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:28.320
It's Re:vale's fifth anniversary.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.120
We'll leave it up to you guys.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.510
I can't believe we'll be seeing 
such dreamlike units onstage.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:35.000
I'm already excited.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.500
That's great.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.130
By the way, I heard there's 
another plan in the works.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.000
That's right.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.510
We're thinking of singing 
"Dis one." as our last song.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.300
What?!

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.090
You mean Zero's big hit?

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:52.190
You're going to cover it?

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:56.080
Yeah. We'll be selling advance copies of 
our single at the inaugural show, as well.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:58.810
We plan to play it during 
Zero Arena commercials, too.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.070
It should start airing soon.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.290
You're taking a crack at Zero?

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.820
That's daring of you.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:08.030
You really do make bold moves.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:12.170
It's not like we aspire to surpass Zero.

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.670
Zero is so exceptional, 
no one's covered his music.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:20.420
Since he's got so many hardcore fans, 
it's always possible there'd be backlash.

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:24.620
But if Re:vale covers him, 
who could possibly complain?

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:25.970
You're right.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:30.350
The Zero Arena where Zero last 
performed is being renovated.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:33.240
We want to sing Zero's song there.

00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:36.860
If we don't, it'd feel like 
his songs were wasted.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.610
Besides, you'll never get anything 
done if you fear backlash.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.720
And we need to encourage our 
juniors to be courageous.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.090
Sounds like Re:vale.

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:49.620
You've been kind to TRIGGER, too.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.290
You have our full support.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.520
Thank you.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.580
Okay, everyone. Lend me your hands.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.340
Re:vale, TRIGGER, IDOLiSH7.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.830
RTI for short!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:09.300
Let this be a huge, huge, huge, huge,
 huge, huge, <i>huge</i> success!

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.720
Ready...

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.760
<i>MEZZO"'s...</i>

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.360
<i>Let's...</i>

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.960
...<i>Run Away Together (Again)</i>!

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.880
<b>Let's Run Away Together (Again)</b>

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.500
<i>Today the MEZZO" duo has come to</i>

00:13:23.000 --> 00:14:32.760
Great for Rabbinsta! 
Stylish sweets popular among young people!!

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.280
<i>the popcorn stand all the high 
school girls are talking about.</i>

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:33.510
<i>What's this? Tamaki-san seems 
to be eating some already.</i>

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:35.190
So good!

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.980
There are 15 varieties of popcorn flavors.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:41.550
Including limited seasonal varieties, 
there are more than 20 total—

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.050
Come on, So-chan. Open wide.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.060
I'm in the middle of talking.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.500
Actually, you can't have any.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.890
<i>Tamaki-san, you're incorrigible.</i>

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.980
Whoa, that'll look awesome on Rabbinsta!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.690
Wait, Tamaki-kun!

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:02.690
Sorry about that.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:03.880
It's fine.

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:08.050
These cotton candies really are cute.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.990
And they're decorated with...

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.790
So-chan, open wide. Say, "ah."

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:14.360
What?

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.750
I'm not in the shot.

00:14:20.010 --> 00:14:24.150
<i>This walk around town 
will continue next week.</i>

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.300
Tamaki-kun!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:30.540
<i>Tamaki-san, let Sogo-san have 
some sometimes, okay?</i>

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:38.180
<b>Let's Run Away Together (Again)</b>

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:35.670
Here's today's runaway comments.

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:37.040
Tamaki-kun, if you please.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:38.180
Who, me?

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Let's Run Away Together (Again)</b>

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:39.940
<b>Today's Runaway Comments</b>

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:43.690
"Wandering around together 
once in a while isn't so bad.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:47.520
Absent-mindedly, aimlessly, nonchalantly."

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.950
You weren't nonchalant at all, though...

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:59.460
<b>Let's Run Away Together (Again)</b>

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:53.730
It's your fault for not 
trying to eat anything.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.400
See you next week!

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.460
Okay, cut!

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:02.330
Thank you.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.730
See you again next week.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.170
Thanks.

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:08.220
Tamaki-kun, listen...

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:10.720
What? More criticisms?

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.780
Even on-location shoots 
have to follow a plan.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.570
You can't keep latching 
on to everything you see.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.100
Who cares? That stuff did great on Rabbinsta.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:27.360
<b>Let's Run Away Together (Again)</b>

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.650
I'm sorry.

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:24.090
It's fine, as long as it's interesting.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.640
We'll be more careful in the future.

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.890
Sure, thanks.

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:29.720
Tamaki-kun.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:31.990
I know, jeez.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.030
Um, excuse me...

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.630
You're Osaka Sogo-san of MEZZO", aren't you?

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.130
Huh? Yes, that's me.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:52.320
Um...

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:57.140
Is Yotsuba-san not with you?

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:58.330
Um...

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.850
Is he doing well?

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.940
What? Yes, he is.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.310
That's good. That's fine, then.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:11.740
Do you know Tamaki-kun? 
Could I get your name?

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.110
Oh, I...

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.610
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:21.000
<i>She seems kind of like 
Tamaki-kun, in a way...</i>

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:25.710
Wait, are you Aya-chan?

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:29.520
No! Please don't tell anyone you met me!

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.830
What? Why not?

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:33.340
Forget why! If you do, I'll jump!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.090
Jump?! From where?

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.470
Somewhere high that would kill me!

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:38.010
Wha—

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:39.220
Excuse me!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:41.600
Hey, wait!

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:51.980
Isn't this...

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:54.740
Thank you.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:57.990
Hey, Nagi.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.490
Mitsuki!

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.940
Did you finish your meeting?

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:06.680
Yeah. I thought I'd do a bit of 
shopping before heading home.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.920
I'll join you!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.770
What are you talking about?

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.630
Don't you have a shoot with 
Clara Lowell after this?

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.810
Oh, you're right...

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:21.880
Mitsuki, you're in great demand these days.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.060
I'm glad you seem to be doing well.

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:26.830
That makes two of us.

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:31.610
I finally feel like I'm useful instead 
of being a burden to everyone.

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:35.510
Why? I've never thought of you as a burden.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:38.350
You certainly do look like 
you could be carried, though.

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:40.540
Oh.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:41.240
Shut up.

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:45.570
I guess it's not like that.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.690
I don't have to be the best.

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:50.770
I don't need to be popular.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.900
I know I never could be.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:56.090
But I wanted to be useful without relying on

00:17:56.090 --> 00:18:00.370
Riku's singing, your looks,
or the strengths of the other members.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.690
Mitsuki.

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:05.310
I feel like I can finally be confident 
from the bottom of my heart

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:10.560
and say I'm Izumi Mitsuki of IDOLiSH7.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:14.320
Hey, I'm useful to the rest
of the guys, right?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.520
Of course you are!

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.450
Good.

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:20.140
I'm off, then.

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.010
I'm going to splurge and reward myself.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:25.700
See you later. Have fun!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.530
This sweater...

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.730
Hey, did you see <i>Lovely Night
With You</i> the other day?

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:57.260
Yeah. It was so good!

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:59.240
It's how I de-stress these days.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.120
I wish I could see next week's episode now.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.530
Awesome. I'm going to tell
the others when I get home.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:06.740
Don't you feel like Mitsuki 
gets in the way, though?

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.500
He's not even the center, 
but he runs the show.

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:16.370
I wish the other members would talk 
more, but he interrupts too much.

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:19.040
I know what you mean.
I don't care about the older Izumi.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.000
Just show me Riku-kun!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:24.470
He's not even popular.
I wish he'd read the room.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.480
Right?

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:30.270
Sir, if you'd like, you could try that on.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.600
Are you Izumi Mitsuki-san of IDOLiSH7?

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:36.290
No.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:36.690
What?

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.680
No, you have the wrong person.

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.640
I'm not him.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:42.700
Sir?

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.570
Excuse me.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.360
<i>I don't want anyone to find me.</i>

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.320
<i>Not because I'm a celebrity.</i>

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.590
<i>I don't want to be laughed at.</i>

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.120
I thought I could finally say it.

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.610
That I'm Izumi Mitsuki of IDOLiSH7.

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.110
I thought I could finally say it...

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:44.260
It's no use. I cough so 
easily this time of year.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.600
You cannot do this job.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:52.520
You should quit being an idol.

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.640
I know what Tenn-nii said,

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.300
but I really like this job.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:01.380
Maybe I'm being selfish...

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.530
I'll stop thinking about it for now.

